From 6d307cdb75a612feba4b1c4edc617692bbb60378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <mexicouger@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:40:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add scene post-process: screen-space shadows, bump mapping,
 specular

Fast3D transforms vertices on the CPU and discards world positions and
normals, so a shadow-map pass would mean running every display list twice.
Instead add an optional fullscreen pass over the finished world that
rebuilds world-space positions from the depth buffer.

* New display list command G_SCENEPOSTFX (0x4b) / gSPScenePostFx(), carrying
  a ScenePostFxParams (sun direction, shadow and bump settings).
* Interpreter captures the latest perspective view-projection and, when the
  gScenePostFx.Enabled CVar is set, renders through the game framebuffer.
* GfxRenderingAPI::ApplyScenePostFx() (default: unsupported). Implemented
  for OpenGL and OpenGL ES 3.0 (GLSL ES 300 / 130 / 410 core).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CAmUXgE1XrEo1hGsHciUoa
